# Rule 3: Naukri sidebar filters must click + reconfirm

When applying Cosmo prefs on Naukri search, **Salary**, **Location**, and **Work mode** under All Filters must actually tick — keyword-only search is not enough. After clicking, **reconfirm** via checked inputs and/or URL params before scanning.

## Real DOM (do not guess)

```html
<div class="styles_chckBoxCont__…">
  <input id="chk-10-15 Lakhs-ctcFilter-" type="checkbox" style="display:none" />
  <label for="chk-10-15 Lakhs-ctcFilter-">
    <i class="ni-icon-unchecked"></i>
    <span class="styles_filterLabel__…" title="10-15 Lakhs">10-15 Lakhs</span>
  </label>
</div>
```

- Filter ids: `*-ctcFilter-` (salary), `*-wfhType-` (work mode), `*-cityTypeGid-` (location)
- Containers: `[data-filter-id="salaryRange"]`, `[data-filter-id="wfhType"]`, `[data-filter-id="citiesGid"]` / `cityTypeGid` / `location`
- Higher salary bands / more cities need **View more** first
- Location aliases: Bangalore↔Bengaluru, Hyderabad↔Hyderabad/Secunderabad

## Click requirements

1. Prefer finding by `input[id*="ctcFilter"]` / `input[id*="wfhType"]` / `input[id*="cityTypeGid"]` + title/label text
2. Never treat a lone `styles_filterLabel` span as the click target row without walking up to `chckBoxCont` / `label`
3. Native `input.click()` alone fails (`display:none`) — use a full **pointerdown → mouse → click** sequence on the **label / icon / chckBoxCont**, with React `onChange` fallback
4. Do not match page copy like "Remote jobs"; scope to filter options
5. Verify with `input.checked` / `ni-icon-checked` after click; retry if it did not stick
6. Reconfirm with `confirmPreferenceFilters` (sidebar + URL `ctcFilter` / `l` / `cityTypeGid` / `wfhType`) before treating filters as done
